From b18249d036cafb18210254291e4d18bc99023d42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 14:19:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] subsys/pmci/mctp: add MCTP-over-serial binding (DSP0253),
 interrupt-driven

Add a DMTF DSP0253 MCTP-over-serial transport binding driven over the
interrupt-driven UART API (uart_fifo_read / uart_fifo_fill), plus a PLDM
Type 0 sample that bridges a Zephyr QEMU instance to an OpenBMC QEMU
instance over a host unix socket.

The wire framing (0x7e flags, 0x7d byte stuffing, RFC1662 FCS-16) is
identical to the existing async mctp_uart binding, but the I/O path uses
only the interrupt-driven UART API, so it runs on controllers without
async/DMA support -- notably the SiFive UART on QEMU's sifive_u machine,
which is the practical inter-QEMU MCTP path today.

Notes on the SiFive UART: irq_is_pending()/irq_tx_ready() report the raw
hardware condition (TXWM stays asserted while the TX FIFO is below the
watermark) and irq_update() always returns 1, so the ISR runs a single
pass and gates the TX FIFO behind a tx_active flag rather than looping on
irq_is_pending().

The serial_bridge sample registers the PLDM Type 0 responder as EID 18
and answers GetTID / GetPLDMTypes / GetPLDMVersion from the BMC (EID 8).
The board overlay redirects zephyr,sram from l2lim to ram0 (DDR) so the
image boots on QEMU's sifive_u model, which does not implement l2lim.

Verified end-to-end against a host DSP0253/PLDM simulator over a
-serial unix: socket:

  GetTID         -> cc=0x00 tid=1
  GetPLDMTypes   -> cc=0x00 type0 supported
  GetPLDMVersion -> cc=0x00 1.0.0
